{"id": "EUVD-2026-101230", "enisaUuid": "62f7e7b1-7fc9-3863-96a8-6eca53fe5a70", "description": "libmspack through 0.11alpha contains an uninitialized pointer free vulnerability in kwajd_open() in mspack/kwajd.c that frees unzeroed filename and extra pointers on header read errors. Attackers can supply a truncated, empty, or wrong-signature KWAJ file to crash the process or obtain an arbitrary-free memory corruption primitive.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:01:09", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/kyz/libmspack/commit/4d868504114346aa767d435fbb89a8b76603493f", "https://github.com/kyz/libmspack/blob/v0.11alpha/libmspack/mspack/kwajd.c#L111-L181", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libmspack-kwaj-uninitialized-free", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libmspack-through-0-11alpha-uninitialized-pointer-free-via-kwajd-open-error-path"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110602", "GHSA-5m37-fqj8-q94j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9381f911-b828-3053-8f07-33a01c63cdce", "product": {"name": "libmspack", "vendor": {"name": "libmspack"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.11alpha"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f3161adc-913e-3c44-b488-6663d312c7ca", "vendor": {"name": "kyz"}}], "isExploited": false}